@zen_marten84: For large JSON files, I use `ijson` with streaming parsing—way better than loading the whole thing into memory. It’s a bit more verbose but saves RAM and avoids OOM crashes. If you need nested structure, `ijson.items()` lets you iterate over objects or arrays safely.  

Trade-off: slightly more complex code vs. 80%+ memory savings. For high-throughput apps, it’s worth it.  

Avoid `json.load()` on files >100MB. Even `json.loads()` with chunks can backfire—streaming wins every time.

